  "reconstructed_theorem_text": "Let E be a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure, and let S be an arbitrary measurable space. Dimension zero for E is allowed; there is no Nontrivial or nonempty-S assumption. Let V:E->R and kappa:R satisfy kappa>=1, V is twice continuously Frechet differentiable, and for every x,v in E,\n  kappa^(-1)*||v||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x v) v <= ||v||^2.\nLet eta:S->R and y:S->E be measurable, and assume for every s in S that 0<eta(s)<=1. The norm is the given real Hilbert norm and grad V is the genuine Riesz representative of the Frechet derivative.\nDefine, for every s in S and x in E,\n  F(s,x)=V(x)+(eta(s))^(-1)/2*||x-y(s)||^2.\nThen there exists a single map p:S->E such that all the following hold simultaneously:\n(1) p is measurable.\n(2) For every s in S,\n  p(s)+eta(s)*grad V(p(s))=y(s),\nwhere the product eta(s)*grad V is real scalar multiplication in E.\n(3) For every s in S and z in E, both\n  F(s,p(s))+(kappa^(-1)+(eta(s))^(-1))/2*||z-p(s)||^2 <= F(s,z),\nand\n  (F(s,z)<=F(s,p(s))) if and only if z=p(s).\nThus the displayed map is the actual unique global minimizer in each fiber, with the stated strictly positive quadratic growth coefficient; these are conclusions, not supplied minimizer certificates.\n(4) For every s,t in S, if eta(s)=eta(t), then\n  ||p(s)-p(t)|| <= ||y(s)-y(t)||.\nFor this same p define the literal map G:S x E->E by\n  G(s,z)=grad V(p(s)+sqrt(eta(s))*z),\nwith real square root and real scalar multiplication. Then additionally:\n(5) G is measurable on the product measurable space S x E.\n(6) For every s,t in S and z,w in E, if eta(s)=eta(t), then\n  ||G(s,z)-G(t,w)|| <= ||y(s)-y(t)||+sqrt(eta(s))*||z-w||.\n(7) There exists a measurable kernel K:S->Measure(E) which is a Markov kernel (every K(s) is a probability measure), and for every s in S,\n  K(s)=(stdGaussian E).map(z -> G(s,z)).\nHere stdGaussian E is the actual canonical centered covariance-identity Gaussian law in the given finite real Hilbert metric, and map is its literal measurable pushforward. Thus K is the law of the gradient evaluated at p(s)+sqrt(eta(s))*Z for canonical Gaussian Z. It is not asserted to be Gaussian itself, a posterior sampling law, or another transition kernel.\nThe order of quantifiers is: arbitrary E,S,V,kappa,eta,y satisfying the stated premises; one measurable p; all optimality/growth/uniqueness and equal-step comparison claims for that p; the let-defined G using that p; measurable G and all equal-step comparison claims; one Markov K with exact law for every s. No probability law on S, independent sampling sequence, joint continuity in eta, comparison between unequal eta values, posterior identity, approximation/error estimate, query count, or whole-algorithm conclusion is present. The coefficients are exactly 1/2 on each quadratic term, 1 on the center-distance bound, and sqrt(eta(s)) on the noise-distance bound. The upper curvature bound 1 and eta cap 1 remain explicit premises even where a particular conclusion could have a wider validity range.",
  "reconstructed_text_sha256": "6179f34ad7ef80c39699a57a41c1e21b35f14fda623831d5fd4b685c6c204eba",
  "objects": "Actual C2 scalar potential V; positive real step-size field eta and center field y; F(s,x)=V(x)+(eta(s))^-1/2*||x-y(s)||^2; one measurable minimizer map p; genuine Riesz gradient; literal G(s,z)=gradient V(p(s)+sqrt(eta(s)) scalar-multiplied z); canonical stdGaussian E; measurable Markov kernel K equal fiberwise to the Gaussian gradient-output pushforward.",
  "domains": "E:Type with NormedAddCommGroup,InnerProductSpace R,CompleteSpace,FiniteDimensional R,MeasurableSpace,BorelSpace; full real Hilbert carrier, including dimension0. S:Type with only MeasurableSpace, arbitrary and possibly empty. V:E->R,kappa:R,eta:S->R,y/p:S->E,F:S->E->R,G:SxE->E,K:Kernel S E. All directions/points/noise variables range over E, every index over S; G uses the product sigma-algebra. No measure on S is given.",
  "quantifiers": "Universal ambient types/structures,V,kappa,eta,y under all assumptions. Global curvature:every x,v:E. Step constraints:every s:S. Exists ONE p:S->E before all following conjuncts:Measurable p;every s optimality;every s,z BOTH quadratic growth and the <= iff equality characterization;every s,t equal-eta implies p comparison. LET G from that same p;Measurable G;every s,t,z,w equal-eta implies G comparison. Exists ONE K:Kernel S E,IsMarkovKernel K AND every s exact pushforward equality. K follows the same p/G; not separately selected per index.",
  "assumptions": "kappa>=1;actual ContDiff R2 V;for all x,v kappa^-1||v||^2<=fderiv R(fderiv R V)x v v AND fderiv R(fderiv R V)x v v<=||v||^2;Measurable eta;Measurable y;for every s eta(s)>0 and eta(s)<=1. Structural finite complete real Hilbert/Borel conditions on E and measurable S. Equal eta(s)=eta(t) is a premise in EACH pair comparison, not a global constancy assumption. No pre-supplied minimizer,gradient regularity certificate,probability normalization,posterior moment,or algorithm estimate is assumed.",
  "conclusion": "Exists measurable p with every-s p(s)+eta(s) scalar-multiplied gradient V(p(s))=y(s). For every s,z:F(s,p(s))+(kappa^-1+(eta(s))^-1)/2||z-p(s)||^2<=F(s,z) AND (F(s,z)<=F(s,p(s)) iff z=p(s)). For all s,t with equal eta,||p(s)-p(t)||<=||y(s)-y(t)||. For literal G from p:Measurable G AND every s,t,z,w with equal eta,||G(s,z)-G(t,w)||<=||y(s)-y(t)||+sqrt(eta(s))||z-w||. Exists Markov K and for all s,K(s)=stdGaussian E.map(z->G(s,z)). Every conjunct is retained; no uniqueness measurability supplied as premise.",
  "scopes": "The growth and equality characterization imply true unique global fiber minimizers. Full-range carrier E is used for curvature and all points/noise. The two Lipschitz-style comparisons cover ONLY pairs with equal eta; no unequal-step or joint eta-continuity bound is stated. Kernel existence is a genuine measurable Gaussian gradient-output family,not a posterior/RGO/HMC law or an assertion that its pushforward is Gaussian. There is no law on S,random-history algorithm,approximation/work/transition-invariance/transport bound,or main theorem conclusion. Zero-dimensional E is included. The supplied definitions are sufficient; ambiguity is null.",
  "constant_dependencies": "kappa>=1 ensures kappa^-1>0; each eta(s)>0 and <=1. Exact regularizer coefficient=(eta(s))^-1/2. Exact growth coefficient=(kappa^-1+(eta(s))^-1)/2. Hessian upper coefficient1 is explicit. Center comparison coefficient1; G comparison coefficients1 and sqrt(eta(s)),only under eta(s)=eta(t). Gaussian covariance is identity in E; no dimension,partition,trace,quarter factor,or hidden error constant appears. These are pointwise deterministic estimates and exact probability-law equality,not asymptotic rates.",
